    "body": "What's the runtime cost of running `kubectl`, especially if your caches are empty?\r\n\r\nMost of our modules are gated behind the existence of files, which is a relatively quick check, then a more expensive call to runtimes if the appropriate files are found. Without that, we'd be forking a process for each module every time we ran the shell, which isn't exactly *slow* individually, but adds up.\r\n\r\nIs there the presence of some sort of file/envar or other quick check we could use as a fast check before running kubectl?",
